WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.086 --> 00:00:11.938
"I hope Alpha is recalibrated by now," Ally thought as she raced home from work.

2
00:00:11.939 --> 00:00:15.267
She'd just walked through the front door when her phone pinged.

3
00:00:15.268 --> 00:00:21.452
Now that Alpha was inside the new computer, Ally's new phone was working great for calls and texts.

4
00:00:21.453 --> 00:00:25.169
She saw a message from Julius.

5
00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:30.194
Julius: Hi, Ally! My plane got delayed so I just got to Grandma's this morning.

6
00:00:30.195 --> 00:00:33.766
Ally: How is it? Are you having a good time so far?

7
00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:40.066
Julius: It's great. All of Grandma's friends watched Food Truck Rally, and they can't believe that I know the winners.

8
00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:43.026
They all said you were their favorite on the team.

9
00:00:43.027 --> 00:00:46.338
You're famous, people want to know all about you!

10
00:00:46.339 --> 00:00:48.736
"Oh no!" Ally thought.

11
00:00:48.737 --> 00:00:51.766
"I don't want people asking questions about me!

12
00:00:51.767 --> 00:00:57.274
Although, without my powers, no one would believe I'm an alien anyway!"

13
00:00:57.275 --> 00:01:01.873
Ally didn't want to type that, so she sent a smiley face emoji.

14
00:01:01.874 --> 00:01:04.266
Julius: How's everything back in Sandville?

15
00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:06.616
Ally: Good. Busy, today was . . .

16
00:01:06.617 --> 00:01:10.098
Bong! A loud noise came from her room.

17
00:01:10.099 --> 00:01:14.483
"Alpha!" Ally ran into her room.

18
00:01:14.484 --> 00:01:17.383
Ally: Can I text you later? Alpha . . .

19
00:01:17.384 --> 00:01:19.852
She quickly deleted the word.

20
00:01:19.853 --> 00:01:25.636
Ally: My new computer just booted up!

21
00:01:25.637 --> 00:01:30.766
Just then Ally heard another sound—the sweetest one ever.

22
00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:39.650
"Greetings. I am Alpha CXB unit serial number 7638hbc81 at your service."

23
00:01:39.651 --> 00:01:41.175
"You're back, Alpha!

24
00:01:41.176 --> 00:01:45.130
Are you fully functional?" Ally crossed her fingers.

25
00:01:45.131 --> 00:01:48.996
"Some memory files must still be restored," Alpha said.

26
00:01:48.997 --> 00:01:55.479
"Due to the primitive nature of this Earth technology, progress is slow, but I am ready to serve."

27
00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:58.251
"I'm so happy, I could hug you!"

28
00:01:58.252 --> 00:02:01.201
Ally rushed to throw her arms around the computer.

29
00:02:01.202 --> 00:02:02.571
Beep! Beep!

30
00:02:02.572 --> 00:02:10.110
"Halt, Allyzooba! That is human behavior—an inappropriate response for an Astralian!" "You're

31
00:02:10.111 --> 00:02:12.766
right." Ally hung her head. "I

32
00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:15.150
don't want to be human. I

33
00:02:15.151 --> 00:02:20.726
want to be an Astralian, one who makes her parents proud one day." "That

34
00:02:20.727 --> 00:02:23.825
is admirable," Alpha said. "My

35
00:02:23.826 --> 00:02:27.010
memory banks have retrieved an old request from you. You

36
00:02:27.011 --> 00:02:29.807
wanted me to help you find your powers. Confirm

37
00:02:29.808 --> 00:02:33.341
this situation has been corrected." "It

38
00:02:33.342 --> 00:02:37.322
hasn't!" Ally sighed. "I

39
00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:41.061
still need your help getting them back. It

40
00:02:41.062 --> 00:02:46.997
happened right after I watched the lunar eclipse at the park." "Issue

41
00:02:46.998 --> 00:02:49.481
located," Alpha said.

42
00:02:49.482 --> 00:02:55.049
"Astralia has no moon. Therefore, there are no lunar eclipses."

43
00:02:55.050 --> 00:03:00.253
"I know that," Ally said. "What does that have to do with my problem?"

44
00:03:00.254 --> 00:03:06.475
"Astralians can be affected by maladies when exposed to lunar eclipses." Alpha frowned.

45
00:03:06.476 --> 00:03:11.335
"This is basic information taught to young Astralians in first grade."

46
00:03:11.336 --> 00:03:16.396
Ally gulped. "I really should have paid more attention in school.

47
00:03:16.397 --> 00:03:20.810
I never would have gone outside during the eclipse if I'd known that."

48
00:03:20.811 --> 00:03:26.273
"You also would have learned how to fix the maladies in the same lesson," Alpha said.

49
00:03:26.274 --> 00:03:28.927
"What do you mean?" Ally asked.

50
00:03:28.928 --> 00:03:32.280
"Viewing a solar eclipse will reverse the effects.

51
00:03:32.281 --> 00:03:37.827
However, it is dangerous to view a solar eclipse without proper eye protection."

52
00:03:37.828 --> 00:03:41.415
"I'll get some! Whatever I need!" Ally said.

53
00:03:41.416 --> 00:03:44.179
"When is the next solar eclipse?"

54
00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:47.888
"Eclipses occur in pairs on Earth," Alpha said.

55
00:03:47.889 --> 00:03:52.445
"The next solar eclipse is due to occur in exactly five days."

56
00:03:52.446 --> 00:03:56.664
"Great news!" Ally did a little happy dance.

57
00:03:56.665 --> 00:03:59.161
"I knew you'd figure it out!

58
00:03:59.162 --> 00:04:02.256
I'll have my powers back by next week!"

59
00:04:02.257 --> 00:04:06.142
"Affirmative," Alpha said. "However, there is one—"

60
00:04:06.143 --> 00:04:10.752
"Argh!" Mateo shouted in the hallway outside Ally's door.

61
00:04:10.753 --> 00:04:15.846
Ally threw open her door and saw Mateo standing there with his tablet in his hands.

62
00:04:15.847 --> 00:04:19.064
"What happened, Mateo? Are you all right?"

63
00:04:19.065 --> 00:04:22.330
"No!" Mateo wailed.

64
00:04:22.331 --> 00:04:25.821
"Where are you hurt? Should I call an ambulance?"

65
00:04:25.822 --> 00:04:29.093
Mateo shook his head, looking miserable.

66
00:04:29.094 --> 00:04:33.107
"No doctor could mend my broken heart now."

67
00:04:33.108 --> 00:04:38.343
"Oh no!" Ally cried. "Did Bethany break up with you?"

68
00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:41.597
"No!" Mateo looked insulted.

69
00:04:41.598 --> 00:04:47.234
"The other bidder won the comic book. The auction is over."

70
00:04:47.235 --> 00:04:52.286
"I'm so sorry." Ally patted Mateo on the shoulder.

71
00:04:52.287 --> 00:04:54.903
"I know how much you wanted it."

72
00:04:54.904 --> 00:04:59.909
"I'll get over this one day," Mateo said, hanging his head.

73
00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:01.983
"Wait." He looked up again.

74
00:05:01.984 --> 00:05:05.095
"Did I hear Alpha's voice? Is she back?

75
00:05:05.096 --> 00:05:08.201
Did she find the answer to getting your powers back?"

76
00:05:08.202 --> 00:05:11.647
"She is and she did!" Ally said.

77
00:05:11.648 --> 00:05:19.597
"All I have to do is go outside during the solar eclipse in five days, and I'll have my powers back."

78
00:05:19.598 --> 00:05:22.234
"Awesome!" Mateo said.

79
00:05:22.235 --> 00:05:26.745
"Let's see what we can find out about that solar eclipse."

80
00:05:26.746 --> 00:05:29.199
He typed into his tablet.

81
00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:32.382
A few seconds later he hung his head again.

82
00:05:32.383 --> 00:05:38.923
"Um, Ally, I have some bad news."

